 # Changelog
 
 Dated, factual, one line per change. Newest first.
+
+## 2026-11-12 - Phase 4, Block E2 (data sourcing, model recalibration, W11 Table 40)
+- E2.0 decisions recorded: the PRIMARY targeting model is the refit without the REQUIRES_TIN feature (business vehicle; AUC 0.946, Entry multiplier 6.55x, interval 5.80-7.14x); the all-features model and the fit without UNCERTAIN items are comparison / sensitivity fits (`targeting_model.json variants`, `outputs/tables/targeting_variants.csv`). `tax_morale.baseline.simplicity` is DATA (Afrobarometer Q46A, reversed, 'information burden only'); `agents.non_earners_zero_income` carries `signoff: approved (John, 2026-11-12)` (register column `john_signoff`); the simulations carry a `status` ('UN-RECALIBRATED - NOT FOR PUBLICATION' until the E2.4 calibration succeeds).
+- E2.1: no measure of enforcement found (searched the Afrobarometer R8 merged and Tanzania codebooks, the FinScope 2023 data map, ILFS 2024 labels, TRA Sixth Corporate Plan and the NBS Tax Statistics Reports); `tax_morale.baseline.enforcement` stays an ASSUMPTION with the search list in `config.yaml afrobarometer.baseline_mapping.enforcement`.
+- E2.2: new `src/03_features/twin_inputs.py` -> `data/processed/tra_registered_taxpayers.csv` (TRA registered taxpayers, Mainland, 2011/12-2023/24: 1.04M -> 6.27M; NBS Tax Statistics Reports 2022/23 and 2023/24, with the 2022/23 restatement 4,697k -> 5,494k kept visible; TRA CP6 definitions of active / dormant business TINs) and `data/processed/twin_inputs.json`; the twin's 8 base parameters are DATA (WDI GDP and population growth, Census 2022, TRA, BoT active mobile-money accounts and payment value / WDI GDP, ILFS 2024 informal earnings and household-enterprise receipts); `twin.growth.mm_users` DATA (BoT CAGR 21%), `twin.default.formalization_policy` CALIBRATED (OLS slope of the TRA series per working-age adult), 5 other dynamics constants ASSUMPTION with rationale. Raw sources in `data/raw/{nbs,tra,bot,tcra}/` (git-ignored; 20 rows added to `SOURCES.csv`); WDI series NY.GDP.MKTP.KD.ZG, SP.POP.GROW, SP.POP.TOTL added to `--fetch`.
+- E2.3: the tax-morale model is recalibrated: `p = expit(alpha + beta x index)`, alpha fitted so that the baseline equals the observed adult TIN rate (3.8281%, exact), beta fitted to the log odds ratios the original model implied for the six solo effects at its old baseline (30.6%); the assumed driver deltas are unchanged. Baseline 3.83%, solo effects 4.71-5.79%, combined 11.26%, naive sum 13.07% (was 30.6% / 35.4-40.4% / 58.2% / 78.0% / and, with the E1 data baselines, 56.5% / 80.5%).
+- E2.4: new `src/04_models/agent_calibration.py` -> `data/processed/agent_calibration.json`: the no-intervention agent simulation is calibrated to the TRA registered-taxpayer trend (indexed to the FinScope 2023 adult TIN rate): 2 free parameters (`agents.conversion_rate` 0.15 -> 0.0070, new `agents.p_comply.intercept` -0.252) against 6 points, Nelder-Mead, RMSE 0.22 pp; parameter correlation -1.00 (not separately identified). New basis class CALIBRATED in the register. Agent-based final registration 71.7% -> 7.3% (7.0% without interventions); tier year 10: 28.2% -> 92.7% not registered, Platinum 24.9% -> 2.5%. Digital twin with the E2.2 parameters: baseline tax-to-GDP 12.47% -> 13.8%, policy 14.74% -> 17.4%.
+- E2.5: new `src/04_models/stage_economics.py` -> `outputs/stats/stage_economics.json`, `outputs/tables/table40_stage_economics.csv`: costs, discounted revenue, NPV and ROI of all six stages (10 years, 10% discount, 5% / 12% sensitivities, annuity factors from the formula), 10,000-draw Monte Carlo with explicit distributions in `config.yaml assumptions: stage.*`, revenue per registrant = statutory tax (Income Tax Act Cap. 332 R.E. 2023 First Schedule) on ILFS 2024 earnings of persons outside the formal net. Replaces the typed Table 40 revenue / ROI; the typed `interventions.*` costs no longer feed any claim. NPV factor fixed in `calculate_cost_benefit` (4.33 was the 5% factor). Dashboard cost / revenue / ROI cards (Entry, Active, Enterprise, Legacy) read the new file.
+- Fix: `finscope_summary.json` `government_trust.overall_trust_score_0_10` (48.76) removed: `gov_3` is the amount of the last government / NGO assistance payment in TZS, not a trust score; published as `government_assistance_last_payment_mean_tzs`.
+- Dashboard: Home chart (recalibrated probabilities), Entry / Active / Enterprise / Legacy stage cards, Enterprise tier numbers.
+- Assumptions register: 198 rows (UNKNOWN 32, ASSUMPTION 74, DATA 27, CALIBRATED 3, RETIRED 62); only C062 remains BLOCKED (16 UNKNOWN agent / tier constants); C008, C054, C055, C069, C078, C061 and C062's flag cleared by the recalibration; C041-C053 and C079 left the BLOCKED list.
+- Tests: `test_tra_series.py`, `test_morale_calibration.py`, `test_agent_calibration.py`, `test_stage_economics.py` (new); `conftest.py`, `test_assumptions.py`, `test_afrobarometer.py`, `test_targeting_variants.py`, `test_idempotency.py` updated.
 
 ## 2026-11-12 - Phase 4, Block E1 (TRA-feasible targeting, leakage review, calibration, W10 tax morale, agent inputs from data, dashboard fallback)
 - E1: `src/04_models/targeting_model.py` adds two restricted variants with the same outcome, population, split, CV design, seeds and metrics as the survey model: CORE (age, sex, region, urban/rural) and EXTENDED (CORE + mobile money + business ownership / main income source); `config.yaml targeting.feature_obtainability` states for each feature why TRA can or cannot obtain it. Held-out weighted ROC-AUC 0.946 (all survey features), 0.884 (EXTENDED), 0.829 (CORE). Outputs: `variants` block in `targeting_model.json`, `outputs/tables/targeting_variants.csv`.
