-C056,PDF p.53 | 5. Portfolio-Level Impact > 5.3 EXTERNAL VALIDATION: CAUSAL EVIDENCE FROM | paragraph block 971,"A propensity-score-matched comparison of mobile money owners against non-owners finds a larger effect once selection bias is corrected for — 9.0 percentage points, up from a naive estimate of 5.94 percentage points.",9.0 percentage points; 5.94 percentage points,model-calculated/causal estimate,COMPUTED,"simulated 10,000-person sample with planted effect (economic_model.py run_causal_inference_analysis lines ~1692-1768) -> economic_model.json causal_inference.psm",RECOMPUTE,W6,"Re-estimate on real FinScope 2023; label as observational, cross-sectional. Auto-matched output value(s): outputs\stats\economic_model.json:/agent_based_simulation/yearly_results[8]/year; outputs\stats\economic_model.json:/digital_twin_baseline/yearly_states[8]/year",,,,,,,values unchanged until W6-W8 replace them (simulated inputs with a planted effect),MODELLED (simulated),economic_model.py run_causal_inference_analysis,BLOCKED,"BLOCKED by 12 UNKNOWN constant(s) (psm x12; e.g. psm.income_log_mean, psm.income_log_sigma, psm.income_scale_tzs). See docs/assumptions_register.csv (blocks_claims).",,"Observational association on the real FinScope respondents (n = 9,915): TIN rate 5.3% among mobile-money users vs 0.01% among non-users (non-user rate low precision: fewer than 10 holders); survey-weighted Firth logit, average marginal effect +4.2 pp (95% CI 3.6 to 4.7); odds ratio 38; 99.9% of TIN holders use mobile money. Not a causal estimate.","COMPUTED (observational, first-pass)","src/04_models/tin_mobile_money.py -> outputs/stats/tin_mobile_money.json, outputs/tables/tin_mobile_money.csv",REPLACED,"The matched comparison (9.0 pp up from 5.94 pp 'naive') was recovered from a planted 6 pp effect in simulated data; retired. The real-data association is reported instead, unadjusted and adjusted, with a CI; no selection-bias-corrected causal claim is made.",,,,REPLACED,
