-C060,PDF p.70 | 3. Technical Description | paragraph block 1169,"Below 8 respondents, the tool refuses an estimate entirely rather than showing a number built on too little evidence — verified live on a genuinely thin cell (Arusha × Traders – agricultural products, n=3). 35 of 124 real cells (28%) genuinely fall below the refusal threshold, so this state is a common, expected outcome of the real data, not a decorative edge case.",8 respondents; n=3; 28%,none,MODELLED (design parameter),hard-coded design parameter in dashboard\tdj_lib\*.py / pages,REMODEL,W12,Prototype design parameter; list it in the assumption ledger / config.yaml.,,,,,,,design / illustrative parameter (unchanged),MODELLED (design parameter),dashboard code (not moved to config),LEDGERED (ASSUMPTION),Listed as an ASSUMPTION row in docs/assumptions_register.csv (location: dashboard code).,,"Below 10 respondents (disclosure rule, config.yaml disclosure.min_base), the tool shows 'suppressed (fewer than 10 respondents)'; 7 of the 124 cells (8-9 respondents) that were shown before are now suppressed.",DESIGN RULE (config),config.yaml disclosure:; dashboard/tdj_lib/benchmark_adapters.py reads it,RECOMPUTED - TEXT TO CHANGE,"The report says 8 respondents; the tool now uses the project-wide threshold 10 and flags estimates resting on fewer than 10 cases as low precision. The verified-live example (Arusha x Traders - agricultural products, n=3) is still suppressed.","Below 10 respondents the tool shows the zone estimate (nine NBS TDHS-MIS 2022 zones; labelled 'Zone estimate: region cell suppressed, fewer than 10 respondents'), and if the zone cell is suppressed too, the national estimate. Of the 42 suppressed region x activity cells, 40 resolve at zone level and 2 at national level; none is left without an estimate.",DESIGN RULE (config),"config.yaml zones:, disclosure:; dashboard/tdj_lib/benchmark_adapters.py",RECOMPUTED - TEXT TO CHANGE,Zones are the survey's own grouping (not official administrative area